  "verbalization": "Insulin Human is implicated in the pathogenesis of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus through a complex network of indications. The evidence suggests that Insulin Human is linked to Diabetes Mellitus (disease) via a direct indication, which in turn is associated with two drugs—Gemigliptin and Teneligliptin—that are indicated for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus. This indicates a potential role of insulin in the development of the disease, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The presence of multiple pathways linking Insulin Human to Diabetes Mellitus highlights the involvement of insulin in metabolic regulation, possibly through its effects on glucose homeostasis. The integration of these indications suggests that insulin may contribute to the pathophysiology of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus, though further research is needed to elucidate the precise mechanisms."
